arkdownBody__v5MYy markdown-body"><h2 id="about-contributing-guidelines" tabindex="-1"><a class="heading-link" href="#about-contributing-guidelines">About contributing guidelines<span class="heading-link-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></h2>
20:<p>To help your project contributors do good work, you can add a file with contribution guidelines to your project repository&#x27;s root, <code>docs</code>, or <code>.github</code> folder. When someone opens a pull request or creates an issue, they will see a link to that file. The link to the contributing guidelines also appears on your repository&#x27;s <code>contribute</code> page. For an example of a <code>contribute</code> page, see <a href="https://github.com/github/docs/contribute">github/docs/contribute</a>.</p>

